ges/8b/8b1286adb93e98a6d7b3ece98100c9ad6a51b39549a849ebfa382f2056d055bc.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}:$ \n\n![](images/1e/1e308a124ef6367ff9c877098b76671ed0a40320edf634298a652f3ab187b40a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{p}$ or ${T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/9b/9bf7e5e7c6ddd8ce5faa8e47529454865cfc41e6525de57a811c7dcf38e46154.png)\n\nAs a result, we get the following diagram:\n\n![](images/b4/b48fdc8f6de1d9cb599b0c9a149c3146f969717301a28d81cde083c3f36e80f3.png)"} :step/id #uuid "0e2b6725-ceb7-511a-9ea0-fbf130e6b8ce" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500443}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500392 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e50955-37f8-51bc-83cc-cb950145c252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472820} {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821} :answer-field/id #uuid "33d25ffd-2c6e-5b5b-99df-560a24530be3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1322f1f2-f4c5-54d8-87cc-355df640d02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472822} {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aeb8409-1020-570b-8cec-0822b2e40889" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} {:answer/id #uuid "78ab4291-cd70-5529-b069-e726e0430998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472825}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebe7e6e-372c-5557-a0e2-e163a4bed7dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183354" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\ge 2.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\le -2.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n- **I.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n- **II.** $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n- **III.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ or if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ if and only if $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "1f22cfa3-1706-5ed4-b34a-d29a0dcfdc50" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500451}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ef3ad1-b4c6-531e-b84c-48a55056695b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/74/74d8f90fd8cdfe0e92c5cdf2adc2565fb52bf23ba38a0e6ce492f0c85d5ed796.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499782} {:answer/id #uuid "565f0406-7dec-56e6-8cea-ffdc6a0be4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b4/b4b73f9f99589ff335b71fccf607b05a14c5323d5733951f8df565f57f4aaea2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499822} {:answer/id #uuid "67861f1d-57dc-59c5-b797-379414b570f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/7d/7d5670ffe9e70a476015016874d6dc8fe8e1d4190ec30c79633ec07ed93f2499.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499853} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1267a6-c309-57ed-a173-cc4e435b75a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/55/5524f1c7273ce34497eef45c424321e7c6909bd253a8e4ab841e3bf69c5f1062.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499930} {:answer/id #uuid "f1af3e8b-ee4a-5778-b989-55dfc4905656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fa/fae78827c0cb157201285727b2d8ae1097ad8dd8fa64de098e889eba3d72f12d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499782} :answer-field/id #uuid "b76db7cd-ccd2-5381-930f-35678b186265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f764222e-7e7e-5e1f-8907-653f8f221162" :question/math-academy-id "q-183381" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1532a8be2697c516d88c262ef2d61429f76d1f16a9137c7203de2ca8b451a37.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/f1/f14a8b0a78145e74cd030e2ea648e74167d1b1c4915c0f1fd97ffc1db0a82430.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/bf/bf67afedc00989576903dca9330f636a997f903b722328dec84db7f847925fce.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](images/ca/cabd18cef1dd073877772c85c3ccec372a9f9658d71d3c278fb673489229657e.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/74/74d8f90fd8cdfe0e92c5cdf2adc2565fb52bf23ba38a0e6ce492f0c85d5ed796.png)"} :step/id #uuid "96444738-ac4a-5f68-b324-679d6b04ba39"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500443 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0b4ea8-c305-52fb-b738-39b52cd65224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is not positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401751} {:answer/id #uuid "0f89fefa-c3c4-5941-854f-f243eb5a7db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x\\in N,$ and $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401752} {:answer/id #uuid "fa092300-5642-58f4-a90f-6ea2281b0263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x\\in N,$ or $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401753} {:answer/id #uuid "064a345b-f5c1-5e19-82b0-253407d0787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ and $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401754} {:answer/id #uuid "54036453-852b-5e55-ab90-eafbae198c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401755} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c6802b-9187-56f8-8a12-dde53fdaa099" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2d8f44ce-e231-5920-980e-3c7663e37fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183349" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x\\in N,$ then  $x$ is positive.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in N.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive."} :step/id #uuid "ceeed64c-373d-5d9e-a393-4194a6869a6f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500392}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500451 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e83ceacd-7bdb-5677-92b5-c8f925ae70c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407596} {:answer/id #uuid "618c6d16-a8d6-56f6-89a7-b0c885f2a8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\{10,20,25,30\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499846} {:answer/id #uuid "72135715-b39e-5cf0-b28b-2945d770d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\{10,20,30\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499864} {:answer/id #uuid "75b72781-8ec0-5deb-8ffe-dd841156e69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\{5,10,15,30,35\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499870} {:answer/id #uuid "c757ac5f-7fce-5299-918a-1f1f438db85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\{25\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499846} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c48ea9-d964-59bd-a88d-64bcb5ade0c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7ea344c4-f70e-5016-bcc7-6af9f4085a8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183376" :question/problem "For the universal set $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35\\},\n$$\n\nfind the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer." :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{5,15,25,35\\}\n$$\n\nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=\\{10,20,30\\}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{25\\}\n$$\n\n \nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=\\{5,10,15,20,30,35\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =\\{5,15,25,35\\}\\cap \\{25\\} \\\\  & =\\{25\\} \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =\\{10,20,30\\}\\cap \\{5,10,15,20,30,35\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30\\} \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =\\{25\\}\\cup \\{10,20,30\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,25,30\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ef08bcf6-0e5a-5046-9f01-123adfa7f106" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500425}}] :activity/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499649}]}
